sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Proposed SWIM probes and Lifeguard refutation
    accDescr: A direct probe may succeed or fall back to bounded helpers. Missing replies start suspicion. Buddy notification permits a newer owner incarnation to refute<br/>otherwise a still-current suspicion expires into a local failure judgment.
    participant A as Observer A
    participant H as Helper H
    participant B as Target B
    Note over A,B: Proposed control exchange<br/>message names are conceptual
    A->>B: Direct probe (attempt, epoch, incarnation)
    alt Matching ACK before direct deadline
        B-->>A: ACK
        Note over A: Probe succeeds<br/>update local health
    else No direct ACK in time
        A->>H: Indirect request (same target, correlated attempt)
        H->>B: Helper probe
        opt Helper has no ACK by negative-reply deadline
            H-->>A: NACK (helper observation only)
        end
        alt Matching helper ACK before attempt deadline
            B-->>H: ACK
            H-->>A: Correlated ACK
            Note over A: Probe succeeds even after a NACK
        else No valid ACK before attempt deadline
            Note over A: Enter Suspect for the captured pair<br/>Start bounded suspicion timer
            A->>H: Disseminate Suspect
            A->>B: Prioritized suspicion notification (Buddy System)
            Note over A,H: Distinct reporters may shorten the deadline<br/>Duplicates never restart the timer
            alt Valid refutation reaches A before suspicion expires
                Note over B: If not leaving, advance own incarnation
                B->>A: Owner Alive with newer incarnation
                B->>H: Disseminate newer Alive
                Note over A: Apply Alive<br/>old timer has no effect
            else No valid refutation in time
                Note over A: Recheck pair and timer<br/>Persist rejection floor before publishing Dead
                A->>H: Disseminate Dead (local failure judgment)
            end
        end
    end
    Note over A,B: Late, unsolicited or superseded responses cannot complete newer work<br/>A valid newer Alive may still recover Dead if the epoch was not closed
